WEBVTT

00:02:00.120 --> 00:02:04.120
I really want to go home

00:02:13.660 --> 00:02:14.520
Whazzat?

00:02:17.030 --> 00:02:17.910
It's a machine!

00:02:18.590 --> 00:02:19.810
What does this mean?

00:02:20.840 --> 00:02:21.740
Pass that here for a moment.

00:02:27.080 --> 00:02:29.110
So that crab was a robot?

00:02:29.390 --> 00:02:30.400
A robot?

00:02:31.150 --> 00:02:33.210
Nope, the crab was real.

00:02:33.740 --> 00:02:36.250
Then why did it have this kind of machine in it?

00:02:37.810 --> 00:02:38.730
I ain't sure.

00:02:39.590 --> 00:02:41.860
I'll try figure it out.

00:02:46.490 --> 00:02:48.400
Chako, let's start looking into it right now.

00:02:48.400 --> 00:02:49.130
Alright!

00:02:59.690 --> 00:03:01.410
Dinner is served!

00:03:02.260 --> 00:03:02.930
I don't need any!

00:03:03.360 --> 00:03:04.410
Go on and eat without me!

00:03:06.230 --> 00:03:08.160
Shingo's sure enthusiastic.

00:03:13.510 --> 00:03:18.420
Maybe this part is some kind of enhancement that supports the movements of the muscles.

00:03:20.140 --> 00:03:20.970
Looks like it.

00:03:21.720 --> 00:03:22.980
It really is.

00:03:28.090 --> 00:03:29.740
Nano-plant?

00:03:33.120 --> 00:03:34.450
I've heard of them.

00:03:35.020 --> 00:03:39.870
To put it simply, they're computers so small you can't see them with the naked eye.

00:03:40.390 --> 00:03:42.610
But we can see that machine, can't we?

00:03:43.090 --> 00:03:44.070
You're quite...

00:03:44.650 --> 00:03:45.330
...the idiot.

00:03:45.940 --> 00:03:46.770
What?

00:03:47.540 --> 00:03:51.440
Basically, lots of little computers attached together to make it.

00:03:51.700 --> 00:03:53.440
It's an organic Integrated Circuit.

00:03:53.780 --> 00:03:55.660
That's what nano-plants are.

00:03:57.700 --> 00:04:00.680
Then that means somebody made that crab after all.

00:04:00.870 --> 00:04:01.810
Wrong!

00:04:03.310 --> 00:04:04.620
The crab was real.

00:04:04.990 --> 00:04:08.800
Someone just put nano-plants into it and was manipulatin' it.

00:04:12.910 --> 00:04:14.050
Which means...

00:04:14.580 --> 00:04:18.330
Someone else other than us is here.

00:04:24.190 --> 00:04:26.180
There's a high possibility of that.

00:04:26.350 --> 00:04:28.980
I'll have to examine those ruins.

00:04:30.140 --> 00:04:32.970
But what was it being manipulated for?

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:37.080
Maybe something important is hidden in those ruins.

00:04:37.580 --> 00:04:39.230
That might be true.

00:04:40.430 --> 00:04:41.280
If you'll excuse me...

00:04:44.050 --> 00:04:45.680
Where are you going, Shingo?

00:04:46.580 --> 00:04:50.410
If I use that machine, I might be able to fix the communication system.

00:04:51.360 --> 00:04:52.680
Is that true, Shingo?

00:04:53.520 --> 00:04:54.380
I'll give it a try.

00:04:59.590 --> 00:05:01.210
If we can transmit...

00:05:01.490 --> 00:05:03.330
...someone will come save us!

00:05:03.360 --> 00:05:04.090
Which means...

00:05:04.540 --> 00:05:06.490
...we can go home! We can really go home!

00:05:06.870 --> 00:05:08.010
Alright!

00:05:08.010 --> 00:05:09.270
We don't know for sure yet.

00:05:10.540 --> 00:05:13.080
That machine has a structure I ain't seen before.

00:05:13.830 --> 00:05:16.920
It ain't clear if we'll be able to use it in the communications system.

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:18.660
Chako!

00:05:20.220 --> 00:05:21.890
Hurry up and come help me!

00:05:23.180 --> 00:05:24.490
I'm on my way!

00:05:25.620 --> 00:05:26.090
See ya.

00:05:28.470 --> 00:05:29.030
Chako...

00:05:30.030 --> 00:05:31.640
Sorry, but we're counting on you.

00:05:32.610 --> 00:05:33.830
Everyone's tired...

00:05:34.260 --> 00:05:35.310
...so we're going to sleep ahead of you.

00:05:36.210 --> 00:05:37.770
Okay! Leave it to us!

00:05:43.730 --> 00:05:45.480
That's crazy processing speed.

00:05:45.700 --> 00:05:49.900
While constantly calculatin', it's adaptin' to the crab's physique.

00:05:50.650 --> 00:05:51.850
How's it doin' it?

00:05:52.340 --> 00:05:53.180
Hey, Chako...

00:05:53.740 --> 00:05:56.440
Maybe we can use this as an incremental amplification circuit.

00:05:56.880 --> 00:05:57.910
Which? Pass it here.

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:00.640
How is it, Shingo?

00:06:00.870 --> 00:06:03.440
How many more minutes is it going to take?

00:06:04.080 --> 00:06:05.330
Just wait a little longer.

00:06:05.840 --> 00:06:08.240
Just go to sleep! Leave it to us!

00:06:09.780 --> 00:06:11.070
Okay, I get it.

00:06:11.330 --> 00:06:12.780
Well, there's no need to be impatient.

00:06:13.470 --> 00:06:16.840
As long as it's fixed by tomorrow morning, there's no problem.

00:06:18.630 --> 00:06:19.840
What a nuisance.

00:06:21.510 --> 00:06:22.540
I'll definitely fix it!

00:06:22.790 --> 00:06:24.740
There's nothing I can't fix!

00:06:47.430 --> 00:06:49.900
So? Is it going well?

00:06:50.690 --> 00:06:52.990
Maybe. I ain't sure.

00:06:53.610 --> 00:06:54.400
How's Shingo?

00:06:54.940 --> 00:06:55.960
He's still at it.

00:06:56.590 --> 00:06:57.910
He ain't left that seat.

00:07:11.880 --> 00:07:14.050
Shingo, you're really working hard, aren't you?

00:07:15.210 --> 00:07:15.940
Stay away!

00:07:16.390 --> 00:07:17.670
You'll distract me.

00:07:17.880 --> 00:07:20.090
But you should take a little break.

00:07:20.310 --> 00:07:21.530
I said leave me alone!

00:07:27.910 --> 00:07:28.710
Luna...

00:07:30.590 --> 00:07:31.920
I'm sorry for shouting.

00:07:36.380 --> 00:07:37.380
Be moderate about it.

00:07:51.890 --> 00:07:53.610
I think it was like this.

00:07:54.510 --> 00:07:56.220
You walked a very complicated path.

00:07:56.910 --> 00:07:58.750
It's because we were led by the voice.

00:07:59.370 --> 00:08:02.560
So that crab was near these ruins?

00:08:04.840 --> 00:08:08.090
The crab, and the voice that only Luna can hear.

00:08:08.730 --> 00:08:10.530
We really do need to investigate it.

00:08:11.030 --> 00:08:12.340
Let's go take another look.

00:08:13.320 --> 00:08:14.310
We'll have to get ready.

00:08:15.230 --> 00:08:16.880
Then let's split up and get started.

00:08:20.610 --> 00:08:22.660
What, is it fixed yet?

00:08:28.750 --> 00:08:30.550
You'll wake Shingo.

00:08:31.470 --> 00:08:32.910
What's up with him?

00:08:33.270 --> 00:08:35.650
And he promised he'd have it done by morning!

00:08:36.270 --> 00:08:37.110
Stop it!

00:08:37.640 --> 00:08:41.240
It looked like he was working straight through until morning, so don't wake him up yet.

00:08:41.820 --> 00:08:43.280
What are you saying?

00:08:43.830 --> 00:08:45.640
Like I said, you'll wake him!

00:08:47.260 --> 00:08:48.590
Sorry, Shingo.

00:08:50.370 --> 00:08:52.080
And you just got to sleep, too...

00:08:52.280 --> 00:08:53.010
I'm fine.

00:08:53.560 --> 00:08:54.700
Chako, let's get started.

00:08:55.080 --> 00:08:57.160
Don't push it, Shingo.

00:09:01.000 --> 00:09:04.410
Well, I'll overlook how you broke your promise.

00:09:05.200 --> 00:09:08.240
But in exchange, you'd better work on it all morning!

00:09:13.580 --> 00:09:14.430
Hey, Luna...

00:09:14.890 --> 00:09:18.060
...are you really going to go to where those ruins were again?

00:09:20.580 --> 00:09:23.240
If the communications system gets fixed, we'll just have to wait to get rescued.

00:09:24.400 --> 00:09:27.420
We won't need to do anything dangerous.

00:09:29.670 --> 00:09:30.270
Luna...

00:09:31.730 --> 00:09:32.460
What's wrong?

00:09:33.120 --> 00:09:34.710
You've been absent-minded lately.

00:09:35.590 --> 00:09:37.810
Actually it's about Shingo...

00:09:38.330 --> 00:09:39.550
About Shingo?

00:09:41.440 --> 00:09:42.340
What kind of kid is he?

00:09:42.760 --> 00:09:44.480
L-- let's see...

00:09:46.600 --> 00:09:49.360
Actually, I don't really know either.

00:09:51.100 --> 00:09:52.090
Really...

00:09:53.540 --> 00:09:57.140
Because Shingo skipped grades to get into our year of school...

00:09:57.140 --> 00:09:58.680
Try harder!

00:09:59.220 --> 00:10:01.810
...and he's two years younger than everybody else...

00:10:02.140 --> 00:10:04.770
...so he couldn't fit in with everyone.

00:10:06.780 --> 00:10:08.860
I'm spent. Let's take a break.

00:10:09.960 --> 00:10:11.010
It's no use...

00:10:11.780 --> 00:10:12.850
So that's how it was.

00:10:19.730 --> 00:10:20.630
How about siblings?

00:10:21.190 --> 00:10:23.990
I know he has a younger brother and sister...

00:10:24.830 --> 00:10:26.860
A younger brother and sister...

00:10:32.610 --> 00:10:34.020
Give me a break!

00:10:38.390 --> 00:10:40.390
How long will it be before it's fixed?

00:10:40.680 --> 00:10:42.870
Like I said, I'm working on it right now!

00:10:43.340 --> 00:10:45.480
It ain't so easy to fix!

00:10:45.720 --> 00:10:47.520
So what you're saying is that you lied.

00:10:47.800 --> 00:10:50.260
And we were all looking forward to it so badly!

00:10:52.080 --> 00:10:57.420
Instead of acting high and mighty and getting us excited over it, tell us iif you can't fix it!

00:10:58.960 --> 00:11:02.690
But I should have expected it from only-machines-for-friends Shingo!

00:11:03.830 --> 00:11:04.920
What's up with that?

00:11:05.910 --> 00:11:07.960
Remember back in school?

00:11:08.500 --> 00:11:11.690
You didn't have any friends but machines!

00:11:13.360 --> 00:11:16.390
It's only natural that you'd be lying about us being able to go home.

00:11:16.960 --> 00:11:18.850
I never said we could go home!

00:11:19.240 --> 00:11:20.140
That's right, that's right!

00:11:20.890 --> 00:11:21.850
Liar.

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:23.010
Shut up!

00:11:23.860 --> 00:11:26.260
Hey, both of you, what's wrong?

00:11:26.860 --> 00:11:28.280
You see, this liar...

00:11:28.660 --> 00:11:29.500
Forget it!

00:11:31.580 --> 00:11:33.060
Shingo, wait!

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:34.210
Shingo...

00:11:37.600 --> 00:11:39.760
The fault's with Howard!

00:11:39.870 --> 00:11:41.840
He's the one who lied.

00:11:42.510 --> 00:11:44.180
He said we could go home, after all.

00:11:44.370 --> 00:11:45.460
He didn't!

00:11:45.660 --> 00:11:48.230
All he said was maybe he could fix th' communication system!

00:11:48.440 --> 00:11:50.560
You misunderstood on your own!

00:11:50.560 --> 00:11:51.850
It amounts to the same thing.

00:11:52.150 --> 00:11:53.880
It's Shingo's fault.

00:12:24.940 --> 00:12:27.510
I really...

00:12:28.790 --> 00:12:30.060
...want to go home!

00:12:47.110 --> 00:12:47.840
Darling!

00:12:49.410 --> 00:12:50.520
Big bro!

00:12:50.690 --> 00:12:51.940
Wow, wow!

00:12:52.450 --> 00:12:53.420
Skipping grades?

00:12:53.970 --> 00:12:57.830
Starting next year, we'll be moving you ahead two years in school.

00:12:58.020 --> 00:13:00.170
Two school years ahead?

00:13:00.170 --> 00:13:03.470
Mathematics, Physics, Chemistry...

00:13:03.470 --> 00:13:05.640
You're doing well in everything.

00:13:06.030 --> 00:13:09.980
Truth be told, this is the first time I've seen a spectacular student like you.

00:13:10.290 --> 00:13:11.830
You're the pride of our school.

00:13:12.530 --> 00:13:13.920
Keep up the good work.

00:13:14.780 --> 00:13:15.320
Okay!

00:13:16.090 --> 00:13:17.350
Dad...

00:13:17.950 --> 00:13:18.810
Mom...

00:13:22.810 --> 00:13:23.950
I should be able to do it!

00:13:24.490 --> 00:13:27.510
With my skill, there shouldn't be anything I can't fix!

00:13:34.660 --> 00:13:35.560
Homesick?

00:13:37.000 --> 00:13:37.880
Probably.

00:13:38.200 --> 00:13:39.270
That explains it.

00:13:39.780 --> 00:13:41.350
I know I'm lonely...

00:13:41.880 --> 00:13:44.160
...so since Shingo's two years younger, it would go double for him.

00:13:45.010 --> 00:13:47.990
What should we do to cheer Shingo up?

00:13:48.700 --> 00:13:51.060
For know, I think we should just leave him be.

00:14:19.770 --> 00:14:24.250
I'll come home. I'll come home, Mom and Dad.

00:14:27.700 --> 00:14:29.030
This won't work either.

00:14:29.710 --> 00:14:30.360
Shingo...

00:14:31.260 --> 00:14:32.580
Take a break already.

00:14:33.040 --> 00:14:33.640
No way!

00:14:34.510 --> 00:14:35.690
I want to fix it!

00:14:36.100 --> 00:14:37.750
More than anything, I want to fix it!

00:14:37.920 --> 00:14:39.830
That don't mean you shouldn't take a nap!

00:14:40.260 --> 00:14:42.480
I can't stay up with you any longer.

00:14:48.210 --> 00:14:50.200
What can I do to fix it?

00:15:00.230 --> 00:15:01.320
Mom...

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.870
I want to go home, Mom...

00:15:13.960 --> 00:15:15.460
You're pretty skilled.

00:15:16.000 --> 00:15:16.840
What's wrong?

00:15:20.630 --> 00:15:21.380
Nothing much.

00:15:21.740 --> 00:15:24.160
Mommy, I want to go home!

00:15:24.590 --> 00:15:26.540
Taking such good care of something like this.

00:15:27.140 --> 00:15:29.950
You must miss suckling at your mother's teat.

00:15:29.950 --> 00:15:30.810
Give it back!

00:15:31.190 --> 00:15:32.140
No way!

00:15:32.440 --> 00:15:34.000
Howard, stop that!

00:15:34.510 --> 00:15:35.910
I heard it clearly!

00:15:36.480 --> 00:15:38.580
Mommy, mommy!

00:15:38.730 --> 00:15:40.130
I'm lonely!

00:15:40.320 --> 00:15:41.430
What's wrong with that?

00:15:42.210 --> 00:15:42.720
That's right!

00:15:43.000 --> 00:15:45.660
Even though you skipped grades, you're still just a little brat!

00:15:46.110 --> 00:15:48.420
When push comes to shove, you can't fix the communications system.

00:15:48.810 --> 00:15:52.390
Crying for your Mommy just shows how useless you are.

00:15:52.900 --> 00:15:54.790
Howard, give it a rest!

00:15:57.870 --> 00:15:58.940
Shingo, wait!

00:16:02.580 --> 00:16:03.060
Sheesh!

00:16:03.720 --> 00:16:06.510
There's no reason to run away just because I told the truth!

00:16:06.790 --> 00:16:08.970
Howard, what are you talking about?

00:16:09.160 --> 00:16:11.630
But I mean, "Mommy!" right?

00:16:13.090 --> 00:16:15.980
You're the one who's always yellin', "Papa!"

00:16:16.090 --> 00:16:18.890
Understand how lonely Shingo feels!

00:16:19.380 --> 00:16:21.810
And calling him useless was too cruel!

00:16:23.090 --> 00:16:23.930
Like I care!

00:16:27.780 --> 00:16:31.060
He's already gone through so many troubles on account of skipping grades.

00:16:31.770 --> 00:16:34.080
Shingo's trying the best he can.

00:16:34.680 --> 00:16:36.890
Denying that that's the case is...

00:16:37.000 --> 00:16:41.610
Ever since we came to this island, he's been working hard for everyone's sake!

00:16:42.100 --> 00:16:42.940
And also...

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:46.510
...no matter who it is, anyone would get uneasy and think about their family!

00:16:47.140 --> 00:16:48.510
You can't laugh at him for that!

00:16:53.200 --> 00:16:54.780
Sorry, I lost sight of him.

00:17:02.460 --> 00:17:08.820
Shingo!

00:17:09.210 --> 00:17:11.780
Hey! Shingo!

00:17:12.480 --> 00:17:20.890
Shingo!

00:17:23.930 --> 00:17:31.150
Shingo! (x4)

00:17:31.540 --> 00:17:32.760
Shingo!

00:17:34.230 --> 00:17:35.710
Where did he go?

00:17:36.060 --> 00:17:39.940
He may be hiding somewhere because he doesn't want to see us.

00:17:40.150 --> 00:17:43.150
He might be hurt worse than we'd thought.

00:17:44.160 --> 00:17:45.780
This isn't a joke!

00:17:46.110 --> 00:17:48.180
I may have said too much then...

00:17:48.460 --> 00:17:50.880
...but it's not like you're the only one who's lonely!

00:17:54.480 --> 00:17:55.560
Maybe he's...

00:18:03.980 --> 00:18:04.840
Like I thought.

00:18:07.730 --> 00:18:09.270
What should we do?

00:18:11.540 --> 00:18:13.490
You, say somethin' to 'im.

00:18:15.680 --> 00:18:17.090
F-- fine.

00:18:28.580 --> 00:18:30.060
Umm, you see...

00:18:32.010 --> 00:18:32.800
Here.

00:18:35.880 --> 00:18:36.910
Shingo...

00:18:49.660 --> 00:18:51.530
Making me worry about you...

00:18:59.630 --> 00:19:00.610
Papa!

00:19:00.960 --> 00:19:04.080
Papa, Papa, Papa!

00:19:04.190 --> 00:19:05.390
I miss you!

00:19:05.500 --> 00:19:10.020
I really, really miss you!

00:19:17.010 --> 00:19:18.160
Alright...

00:19:19.490 --> 00:19:21.780
Luna?

00:19:22.410 --> 00:19:25.280
Mom! Dad!

00:19:25.600 --> 00:19:29.500
I'm very, very lonely!

00:19:33.510 --> 00:19:36.380
Mom! Dad!

00:19:36.720 --> 00:19:40.860
This island's so very scary and I'm afraid I'll die!

00:19:41.740 --> 00:19:44.140
Mom! Dad!

00:19:44.290 --> 00:19:48.330
It's embarrassing, but I've cried!

00:19:48.590 --> 00:19:51.890
Father! Mother!

00:19:51.890 --> 00:19:56.140
This world is beyond my comprehension!

00:19:58.830 --> 00:20:00.960
Y'don't hafta join 'em if y'don't wanna.

00:20:02.760 --> 00:20:03.720
Everyone...

00:20:09.780 --> 00:20:12.530
Mom! Dad!

00:20:12.870 --> 00:20:18.940
I'll definitely fix the communication system and bring everyone home to meet you!

00:20:38.460 --> 00:20:40.080
Hey, you've done enough.

00:20:40.490 --> 00:20:41.820
You can give up already.

00:20:48.080 --> 00:20:48.760
Alright!

00:20:49.530 --> 00:20:50.130
Here we go!

00:20:50.480 --> 00:20:52.080
Yeah, I'm ready!

00:21:15.030 --> 00:21:16.810
Shingo, the emergency beacon!

00:21:17.220 --> 00:21:17.950
Right!

00:21:21.780 --> 00:21:23.050
I wonder if it'll reach them...

00:21:23.500 --> 00:21:25.230
It's definitely going to reach them!

00:21:25.730 --> 00:21:29.050
.em ot emoC

00:21:29.180 --> 00:21:30.440
We're connected!

00:21:30.870 --> 00:21:32.880
We can go home. We can go home!

00:21:33.230 --> 00:21:34.410
They really received it?

00:21:34.410 --> 00:21:37.830
Alright! Alright! Alright!

00:21:40.620 --> 00:21:43.080
If they responded, it means they're coming to rescue us!

00:21:43.260 --> 00:21:44.140
Alright!

00:21:45.760 --> 00:21:46.340
Everyone...

00:21:46.940 --> 00:21:47.950
...this voice...

00:21:49.510 --> 00:21:51.420
...is the one I've been hearing in my head.

00:21:52.430 --> 00:21:53.290
This one?

00:21:54.010 --> 00:21:57.010
Then we didn't make contact with anywhere?

00:21:58.110 --> 00:21:58.940
What?

00:21:59.480 --> 00:22:01.390
What did that voice say?

00:22:01.960 --> 00:22:02.690
I don't know.

00:22:03.140 --> 00:22:03.850
Really...

00:22:07.510 --> 00:22:10.750
But now it's clear that there's civilization.

00:22:11.410 --> 00:22:12.290
That's right!

00:22:13.830 --> 00:22:15.380
Well done, Shingo.

00:22:17.670 --> 00:22:18.720
That's right, Shingo.

00:22:19.110 --> 00:22:22.360
That's right! Shingo's hard work wasn't wasted!

00:22:24.910 --> 00:22:26.010
Did you get dust in your eye?

00:22:26.010 --> 00:22:26.630
No...

00:22:26.630 --> 00:22:27.940
Don't be silly.

00:22:28.560 --> 00:22:30.100
Shingo, thank you!

00:22:30.960 --> 00:22:31.510
Luna...

00:22:38.310 --> 00:22:40.620
Dad... Mom...

00:22:41.110 --> 00:22:43.360
I'll be fine now.

00:22:43.920 --> 00:22:46.620
After all, I have friends.

00:23:03.490 --> 00:23:05.200
What's wrong, Luna?

00:23:05.860 --> 00:23:08.130
Oh no! That's an awful fever!

00:23:08.520 --> 00:23:10.110
Luna, you must be in pain!

00:23:10.790 --> 00:23:12.400
I want to do something to help her!

00:23:12.890 --> 00:23:15.590
After all, Luna's my best friend!

00:23:16.040 --> 00:23:17.840
I'm not just going to sit idly by!

00:23:18.190 --> 00:23:20.460
Nicely said, Sharla!

00:23:20.460 --> 00:23:22.060
You're a real good girl!

00:23:22.280 --> 00:23:23.560
I'm on the verge of tears.

00:23:25.430 --> 00:23:28.470
Next time: There's always a blue sky in your heart.
